    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `salutation` feature: the create-owner request may include a `title` (MR/MRS/MS/DR), and the owner response exposes `salutation` = `title + ' ' + lastName`, or just `lastName` when no title is given.\n\nChanges made:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`**\n   - Added an optional `title` string property to the `OwnerFields` request schema (so it binds on `POST /api/owners`).\n   - Added a read-only `salutation` property to the `Owner` response schema.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `title` column with getter/setter so the value survives to the `GET` read-back.\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a computed `salutation` mapping: `title + \" \" + lastName` when a title is present (non-blank), otherwise just `lastName`. MapStruct maps `title` through both request\u2192entity and entity\u2192response automatically.\n\n4. **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added the `title` column to the `owners` table.\n\nThe DTOs are generated from `openapi.yml` by the OpenAPI generator, and `title` flows through the existing pipeline (the whole `OwnerFieldsDto` is republished by `ValidateRequiredOwnerFields` \u2192 `BuildOwner`), so no new function classes or YAML wiring were needed.\n\nVerification: `AcceptanceTest.coreComposesSalutation` (posts `title=DR`, `lastName=who`, expects `$.salutation == \"DR who\"`) passes, and the full `mvn test` run reports `BUILD SUCCESS` with 0 failures/errors.",
